## B. ID rules

- Mini creation consumes no canonical ID.
- New event cards use the working sequence beginning at the verified next ID, `P-538`.
- Each genuinely new event uses one working P-ID.
- The sequence advances only after a complete new event card is actually added to this mini.
- Corrections and dated addenda to an existing event retain that event’s original ID.
- Duplicate events do not consume a new ID.
- Temporary/tracking aliases are provenance only and never create extra trials or extra P-IDs.
- A working P-ID appearing here is **not** ledger-committed. Final canonical identity is determined on import through the repository’s ledger-backed workflow.
- If GitHub canonical state advances while this mini is active, preserve already-issued working IDs and aliases here; reconcile them transactionally during import rather than silently renumbering historical mini cards.
- Before every future new card, re-check the live allocator/canonical queue for collision or intervening allocation.

